{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on a401386c: move the marker transport off the public Given.\n\nA rule can read the keys of its Given. A key that only Explore adds\ngives a rule another answer than the runtime gives. So the public\nGiven of Explore holds the runtime's keys and no other key.\n\n1. markSelf leaves the public Given. A module-private association in\n   packages/derive carries the provenance callback of ruling 04218678\n   for the actual capability call. A WeakMap by the private context,\n   or a closure, serves. It adds no public export, no runtime\n   callback and no key that a rule can reach.\n2. The runtime path adds nothing, as today. Its draft bytes stay\n   equal, and the oracle's 4,029 answers and its capture stay\n   unchanged.\n3. The walk of d66ce570 stays strict. It makes no exception for a\n   key. Its case now also states that Reflect.ownKeys of the public\n   Given equals the runtime's key list, in the same order.\n4. Apply the same rule to each object that a rule can reach: a key\n   that only Explore adds is a fault. State in the checkpoint that\n   you found no other such key, or list each one.\n\nThe device-command entry name of ruling 04218678 keeps its meaning.\nOnly its carrier changes.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a401386c848b4180535cc5cbd5485a7f3254c389 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:02c1227e7dc1c04a96ab423dd34c58537b63a2f2, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03c2d3b4bab05912804bc48129712cd98f805758, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:06d96cd732ff547fa8959619d6df87c5953f2ded, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0d76705dfdd74d8de0047a7a257da83b75d575e2 and 74 more","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}